.TH OBDFILTER...FORCE_SYNC 4 2026-11-07 Lustre "Lustre Kernel Interfaces"
.SH NAME
obdfilter.force_sync \- commit an OST and free its destroyed objects
.SH SYNOPSIS
.SY
.BI "lctl set_param obdfilter." FSNAME "-OST*.force_sync=1"
.YS
.SS PROPERTIES
.TP
.B Access Permissions
.br
.BR 200 " | " --w-------
.TP
.B Scope
.br
Per-OST device.
.TP
.B Config
.br
Always present on OST devices.
.TP
.B Default
.br
Not applicable, the parameter is write-only.
.TP
.B Valid Range
.br
Any value is accepted and ignored.
.SH DESCRIPTION
Writing to this parameter makes the OST run the delayed free of objects
whose destroy has already committed, and then commit all pending
transactions on the backing filesystem before the write returns.
The value written is ignored.
.PP
This differs from the
.B osd-*.*.force_sync
parameters, which only commit pending transactions and do not run the
delayed object free.
The test framework uses it so that space and quota used by deleted files
are released without waiting for the background free to run.
.SH MODULES
This parameter is in the following modules:
.EX
.RB "obdfilter." FSNAME "-OST*.force_sync"
.EE
.SH EXAMPLES
.PP
Free destroyed objects and commit an OST:
.EX
.RB "oss# " "lctl set_param obdfilter.lustrewt-OST0000.force_sync=1"
.EE
.SH AVAILABILITY
.B obdfilter.*.force_sync
is part of the
.BR lustre (7)
filesystem package since release 2.18.0.
.\" Added in 2.17.51.xxx
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR lctl-set_param (8)
